<!-- open-hai.chtpm — REAL, CHECKED-IN BOOTSTRAP (2026-08-31, xperiments/
     khtpm-generic-dispatch-design.md's own real conversion writeup).
     Launched by button.sh via the shared khtpm_core_render.+x (the
     SAME renderer every other khtpm window uses - no per-app renderer
     for open-hai anymore).

     The ONLY thing that matters here is the <module> tag: it launches
     khtpm_open_hai_manager.+x as this window's own child process
     (same real fork()+execl() mechanism db-hq/events-hq/chat-hai each
     already use for their own managers, reused verbatim via the
     generic launch_module() - see that function's own header comment).
     The manager owns EVERYTHING else - the instant it starts, it
     overwrites THIS EXACT FILE with the real, live projection (real
     sessions/transcript/model/sound/tool-approval state, via its own
     write_chtpm_projection()), which the renderer picks up within one
     tick via its generic capability #1 (reparse_chtpm_if_changed()).

     DO NOT hand-edit the <page> content below - it only exists so this
     file is valid enough to render for the brief moment before the
     manager's first write lands. Everything under <page> is replaced
     immediately and continuously; only the <module> tag is ever read
     (once, at this window's own startup) and left untouched by the
     manager's own regenerated version.

     REAL, NEW 2026-08-31 (later same day) - the manager's own real
     projection now uses a <sidebar>+<panel> dual-region layout (see
     khtpm_core_render.c's own "generic sidebar+panel scroll" section)
     instead of one flat list - real, fixed window size, sessions in
     their own scrollable sidebar, transcript in its own auto-following
     scrolllist inside the panel. This bootstrap's own placeholder
     content below doesn't need to match that shape - it's replaced
     within one manager tick either way. -->
<window label="open-hai" class="">
  <module src="&.widgits/open-hai/ops/+x/khtpm_open_hai_manager.+x"/>
  <page name="main">
    <text id="status" label="starting..."/>
  </page>
</window>
